---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import '@/assets/styles/academic.css'
---

<PageLayout meta={{ title: 'About' }} class='academic-page'>
  <main class='academic-document' lang='zh-CN'>
    <article>
      <header class='academic-heading'>
        <h1>About</h1>
      </header>
      <div class='academic-content' id='content'>
        <p>Hello，my name is 9dots.</p>
        <p>My email address is ninedots0@gmail.com.</p>
        <p>My phone number is +86 19712260939.Feel free to add me on WhatsApp!</p>
        <p>Welcome to follow me on <a href='https://x.com/9dots0' style='color: #0066cc;'>X</a>.</p>
        <h2 id='about-blog'>About Blog</h2>
        <p>
          I write posts in Markdown and build this site with <a href='https://astro.build/'>Astro</a>.
          Astro loads the posts through Content Collections and builds the article pages and the
          chronological index on the homepage.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href='https://www.mathjax.org/'>MathJax</a> renders equations at build time.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href='https://pagefind.app/'>Pagefind</a> powers full-text search across Chinese and
            English posts.
          </li>
          <li>
            GitHub Actions builds the static site and publishes it to GitHub Pages.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</PageLayout>
